{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816040-2e-lodges-as-mystery-cults","id":816040,"title":"2E Lodges as Mystery Cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T06:04:44-08:00","id":816040,"title":"2E Lodges as Mystery Cults","content":"This is just a little thought experiment I thought up, with regards to the Lodges having no tangible benefits (so far). But what if they're reimagined instead as specialized Mystery Cults? There's some justification for that, seeing as it's mentioned that the Lodge of Shields has Wolf-Blooded members, and they happen to outnumber their Uratha counterparts. That said, here's the first Lodge I was thinking of trying out this hack on, the Lodge of the Chronicle from Werewolf: Second Edition.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Lodge of the Chronicle (o to ooooo)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Cahalith; Expression oo; Academics, Investigation or Occult oo<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Founded over 700 years ago, the lodge seeks to preserve the history and knowledge of the Uratha as a whole. Members often display perfect recall and a dazzling understanding of history and lore. They do, however, have an unfortunate tendency to become lost in interesting stories and are often easily manipulated.<br /> <br /> <b>(o)</b> - A chronicler's task of recording the stories of the People is not an easy one, and often requires him to travel extensively. Cahalith who first join the Lodge are expected to either familiarize themselves with the cultures they visit, or to at least keep both eyes open in their journeys. They therefore gain either the Direction Sense or Well-Travelled Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>(oo)</b> - By this level of initiation, the werewolf has likely commemorated the stories of several packs in a given locale. In the process, he has also begun honing his skills of observation. The Cahalith gains one dot in the Trained Observer Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>(ooo)</b> - At this point, other members of the Lodge have begun to cast their attention on the werewolf, or perhaps even earned the favor of Crying Owl itself. Depending on his circumstances, he may fall under the tutelage of a senior Chronicler, or gain a blessing from the Lodge's Totem. He receives either a two-dot Mentor or a Facet from the Gifts of Insight, Knowledge, or Warding.<br /> <br /> <b>(oooo)</b> - The Cahalith who reaches this level of influence in the Lodge is an example for many of its members to follow. Furthermore, Crying Owl sees that your contributions to the Lodge's mission warrants another blessing. The werewolf thus gains a Facet from the Gifts of Insight, Knowledge, or Warding.<br /> <br /> <b>(ooooo)</b> - The greatest Cahalith of the Lodge live and breathe the knowledge they preserve. They have little difficulty recalling any of the exploits of notable figures in Uratha history. This manifests as a limited form of both Eidetic Memory and Encyclopedic Knowledge, with a specific focus on Uratha lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-25-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe